== G: guards. non-negative bound (control) vs negative bound ==
--- G0
  > public atom Sign(int n)
  > Sign(n) when n >= 0 -> :nonneg
  > Sign(n) when n < 0  -> :neg
  rc=0
--- G1
  > public atom Sign(int n)
  > Sign(n) when n >= -5 -> :a
  > Sign(n) when n <= -6 -> :b
  | $W/G1/a.bs:2:13: error: Sign is not exhaustive
  |   no clause matches:
  |     Sign(n) -> ...
  rc=1
--- G2
  > public atom Sign(int n)
  > Sign(n) when n >= 0  -> :nonneg
  > Sign(n) when n <= -1 -> :neg
  | $W/G2/a.bs:2:13: error: Sign is not exhaustive
  |   no clause matches:
  |     Sign(<= -1) -> ...
  rc=1
== L: is the literal -5 the interval -5..-5? (compare with 5) ==
--- L0
  > type Nz = int where value != 0
  > public int Half(Nz d)
  > Half(d) -> 100 / d
  > 
  > public int UsePos()
  > UsePos() -> Half(5)
  rc=0
--- L1
  > type Nz = int where value != 0
  > public int Half(Nz d)
  > Half(d) -> 100 / d
  > 
  > public int UseNeg()
  > UseNeg() -> Half(-5)
  | $W/L1/a.bs:7:13: error: UseNeg hands Half an argument it does not accept
  |   argument 1 is not covered by Half's declared type:
  |     0
  rc=1
--- L2
  > public int Z()
  > Z() -> 10 / -0
  | compile: $W/L2/a.bs:3:11: Warning: evaluation of operator 'div'/2 will fail with a 'badarith' exception
  | %    3| Z() -> 10 / -0
  | %     |           ^
  rc=0
== R: the residual IS writable as a pattern, not as a refinement ==
--- R0
  > public atom F(int n)
  > F(0) -> :zero
  | $W/R0/a.bs:2:13: error: F is not exhaustive
  |   no clause matches:
  |     F(<= -1) -> ...
  |     F(>= 1) -> ...
  rc=1
!!  R1                         refused  (expected accepted)
        | $W/R1/a.bs:2:1: error: this refinement is not a predicate the checker can read
        |   a refinement narrows a type, so the compiler has to be able to
